findings.evidence:
`_summary(..., full_cost=20.0)` and `_metrics(..., T=20)` set full-acquisition cost equal to T in every fixture. That is exactly the case in which the old F3 normalisation (cost / full acquisition) and the new one (cost / T) agree.

Mutation run in scratch/review_I/mut:
- F3 dividing by `baselines.full_acquisition.mean_test_cost` instead of meta.T;
- the E4 cost/T columns dividing by the full-acquisition cost;
- E9 `deployed_cost_over_T` dividing by the full-acquisition cost.

`pytest -q tests/test_reporting_v3.py` still gives `5 passed in 2.03s`. The main change of Task I (cost / T instead of cost / full acquisition) is therefore not tested in any of the three scripts.
